# A mid-stream disconnect_after cut (testdata/faux/behaviour-retry.yaml
# style) followed by a normal follow-up step: the cut retries and the
# reconnected continuation lands as its own text.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-stream-cut-midtext.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE tell me something long
SHOT typed
KEY enter
# "Here is the first half" is transient: once the retry lands, kiln
# replaces the cut partial text with the fresh reply rather than
# appending to it, so this EXPECT must run right after the WAITFOR that
# first observes it, not after the later reconnect/continuation waits.
WAITFOR /Here is the first half/ 20
EXPECT /Here is the first half/
SHOT cut-point
WAITFOR /Reconnected on attempt 2/ 10
SHOT reconnected
WAITFOR /reconnected continuation lands here/ 10
EXPECT /reconnected continuation lands here, safe and sound/
SHOT continuation
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
